course: dictionary
lesson: 224
title: Alkaline: the opposite of acid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Alkaline describes a substance that is the opposite of an acid. Scientists measure this with the pH scale, which runs from 0 to 14. Acids sit below 7, pure water is neutral at 7, and alkaline substances sit above 7.
explain: Context helps you spot the word. «Soap is slightly alkaline and feels slippery» tells you soap is on the alkaline side of the scale, and the slippery feel is a clue about what alkaline things are like.
explain: Indicators show which side a substance is on by changing colour. Alkalis turn red litmus blue. «Strong alkalis like oven cleaner can burn skin badly» warns you that some alkaline substances need careful handling.
fact: Alkaline means having a pH above 7.
fact: Acids have a pH below 7, and pure water is neutral at 7.
fact: Soap, baking soda and bleach are common alkaline substances.
fact: An alkaline battery is a common kind of battery that uses an alkaline chemical inside.
fact: Strong alkalis such as oven cleaner can burn skin, so wear gloves and safety goggles.
exercise: «Soap is slightly alkaline and feels slippery.» What does alkaline mean? | A plant that grows in soil | Pure water with a pH of 7 | A substance with a pH below 7, like lemon juice | *A substance with a pH above 7, the opposite of an acid
exercise: On the pH scale, which number shows a neutral substance such as pure water? | 3 | 14 | 0 | *7
exercise: «Hydrangeas turn blue in acidic soil and stay pink in alkaline soil.» Find and copy the word that means the opposite of acidic. | pink | acidic | *alkaline | soil
test: What colour does red litmus paper turn when it touches an alkali? | *Blue | Yellow | Red | Green
test: Which of these is a common alkaline substance found at home? | Orange juice | *Baking soda | Vinegar | Lemon juice
exam: Why should you wear gloves and safety goggles when using oven cleaner, a strong alkali? | Because it makes plants grow faster | Because it is neutral like pure water | Because it is sweet and sticky | *Because it can burn skin badly
